  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Before you jump deep into that, @rjzamora ,  do you expect it to be more performant that something like below ?\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef agg_count_distinct(df, group_key, counted_key, client): \r\n     \"\"\"Returns a Series that is the result of counting distinct instances of 'counted_key' within each 'group_key'. \r\n     The series' index will have one entry per unique 'group_key' value. \r\n     Workaround for lack of nunique aggregate function on Dask df. \r\n     \"\"\" \r\n     return ( \r\n         df.drop_duplicates( \r\n             [group_key, counted_key], split_out=len(client.scheduler_info()[\"workers\"]) \r\n         ) \r\n         .groupby(group_key)[counted_key] \r\n         .count() \r\n     ) \r\n```",
    "created_at": "2020-03-24T02:24:21Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/rapidsai/cudf/issues/4663#issuecomment-602970891",
    "id": 602970891,
